        "caseStudy": 14,
        "blockName": null,
        "blockType": "relatedCaseStudyBlock",
        "title": "A real example of how I work",
        "framingText": "This is the only published case study I have right now. It isn't specific to full-stack builds, but it shows how I work end to end."
      },
      {
        "id": "6a544f87140e75434aba4ded",
        "blockName": null,
        "faqs": [
          {
            "id": "6a544f87140e75434aba4de9",
            "question": "Why Next.js/Payload instead of WordPress?",
            "answer": {
              "root": {
                "type": "root",
                "format": "",
                "indent": 0,
                "version": 1,
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "format": "",
                    "indent": 0,
                    "version": 1,
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "For real control over rendering: in Next.js I decide exactly what gets served to the crawler and when, without a caching plugin or third-party theme getting in the way. Payload lets me model SEO fields and structured data directly in the content schema, instead of living as external plugin config that can get disabled or break on any update. The result is less bloat, fewer fragile dependencies, and full control over every technical factor that affects rankings.",
                        "type": "text",
                        "version": 1
                      }
                    ],
                    "direction": "ltr"
                  }
                ],
                "direction": "ltr"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "6a544f87140e75434aba4dea",
            "question": "Does this mean migrating the entire existing site?",
            "answer": {
              "root": {
                "type": "root",
                "format": "",
                "indent": 0,
                "version": 1,
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "format": "",
                    "indent": 0,
                    "version": 1,
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Not necessarily. I can evaluate your current stack and propose a full migration if the site is genuinely limited by its platform, or work on targeted improvements if the problem is narrower. A technical audit is a good first step to figure out which one applies.",
                        "type": "text",
                        "version": 1
                      }
                    ],
                    "direction": "ltr"
                  }
                ],
                "direction": "ltr"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "6a544f87140e75434aba4deb",
            "question": "How fast does a site built this way end up?",
            "answer": {
              "root": {
                "type": "root",
                "format": "",
                "indent": 0,
                "version": 1,
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "format": "",
                    "indent": 0,
                    "version": 1,
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "The goal is Core Web Vitals in the 'good' range from launch, not as a target to chase afterward. Deciding the rendering strategy and JavaScript budget at the design stage avoids the performance debt that usually shows up months after launch.",
                        "type": "text",
                        "version": 1
                      }
                    ],
                    "direction": "ltr"
                  }
                ],
                "direction": "ltr"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "6a544f87140e75434aba4dec",
            "question": "Can I see real projects built this way?",
            "answer": {
              "root": {
                "type": "root",
                "format": "",
                "indent": 0,
                "version": 1,
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "format": "",
                    "indent": 0,
                    "version": 1,
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Yes. The case studies on this site show real projects, not mockups. And the very site you're browsing is a live example of this architecture in production.",
                        "type": "text",
                        "version": 1
                      }
                    ],
                    "direction": "ltr"
                  }
                ],
                "direction": "ltr"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
